            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 22 manifest paths. The change in engine/synctrigger/synctrigger.go reduces risk: the log is created 0600 and narrowed with Chmod on open, a non-absolute state dir is refused so nothing is written under the working directory, log fields containing spaces, control characters, quotes or '=' are quoted to prevent log-line forging, and the stderr copy kept for classification is bounded to 64 KiB.",
              "Rotation is best effort. Rename and remove operate on fixed names under the owner-controlled state directory logs folder, with no user-controlled path components, so no traversal or injection is reachable. A concurrent rotation race can lose an older log file but not the line being written, and that behavior is documented.",
              "The outcome field is written unquoted, but it is produced from a fixed set of classifier values, not from external input, so it cannot be used to forge a line.",
              "The refusal of a non-absolute state dir in RunChild returns skip:no-binary, so no binary is resolved relative to the working directory. This closes a path where a relative default binary could have been run.",
              "The remaining paths are golden files with only the log mode changed from 0644 to 0600, tests, usage text, a comment edit, a recorded review receipt and task documentation. They have no runtime security impact."
            ]
          }
        }
